Hash speed on Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6330 CPU @ 2.00GHz (linux7.0.0-38-generic, 112 CPUs), 2026-11-02 09:40:56 UTC
Full run: 96 rounds. Each cell is the mean time per unit (total time over total work), lower is better.

In “A message in one buffer, after other work”, the program hashes, runs other code and reads 128 MiB of memory (at least 1 ms), and hashes again, as a program hashes between its other tasks; the second call, with the write of its input, is timed.
In “Messages one after another, buffers owned”, the program hashes one input after another, as fast as it can, alone and with a second program doing the same at once.

SOLO: one copy of each contender, on one thread.

